1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,540
(Wang Gege as An San)
Curious who the groom would be?

3
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,020
No idea.

4
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:09,840
I thought it was randomly assigned.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,750
It was completely unknown.

6
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,710
Since our show

7
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,590
is supposed to be unscripted,

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:14,820
everything is pretty random,

9
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,030
so I was looking forward to it.

10
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,140
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

11
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:17,710
Rock, paper, scissors.

12
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,430
The winner goes first.

13
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:20,780
Okay.

14
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:21,100
Come on.

15
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,580
Rock, paper, scissors.

16
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:23,840
(Fist, paper, paper)

17
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:24,550
You lost,

18
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:24,940
so you're out first.

19
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:25,820
You three compete.

20
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:27,340
(Lost her chance to be the groom)

21
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,270
Rock, paper, scissors.

22
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,540
(Fist, paper, fist)

23
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:30,820
(Narrowly lost)

24
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,430
You went from wanting to play
Zhang Linghe's sister to his aunt.

25
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,760
How do you feel?

26
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,070
It all happened so suddenly.

27
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,630
(Surprise)
I didn't even have time to process it.

28
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,290
You played a bride
in a short drama before.

29
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,830
How is this bride role different?

30
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,070
The difference is

31
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,550
this was done in one take,

32
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,670
so it was more nerve-racking.

33
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:51,270
It wasn't as relaxed

34
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,830
as being on a drama set.

35
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,870
There was so much uncertainty on set,

36
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,270
so it still felt a little...

37
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,510
like completing a challenge.

38
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,690
If you get another chance
to be on The Truth,

39
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:03,050
what kind of role would you
want to play?

40
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,460
Can I make a wish?

41
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,390
Yes, you can.

42
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:09,750
I'll play the younger sister.

43
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:11,950
Right.

44
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,180
The kind of younger sister
everyone loves.

45
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,590
Everyone's little sister.

46
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:16,060
Yeah.

47
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:17,750
It'd be pretty happy too.

48
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:20,170
(Gong Yingjie as emcee)
Describe your old friend Jinjing's

49
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:22,170
wedding dance in three words.

50
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,870
Elegant yet funny.

51
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,070
Effortless yet hilarious.

52
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:28,390
Funny with

53
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:29,430
a touch

54
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:30,950
of more funny.

55
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:33,270
It's just...

56
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:34,200
(Good)

57
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,470
really good. Yeah, really good.

58
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,510
I heard you've been an emcee before.

59
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:38,870
How was this time different?

60
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,750
(Glamorous)
It was so dazzling today.

61
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,950
The weddings I hosted before

62
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:42,990
were all

63
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:43,780
warm

64
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:44,700
and solemn.

65
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:46,910
But today was really flashy.

66
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,070
So much more dazzling.

67
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,060
It felt different.

68
00:01:49,270 --> 00:01:50,370
And another thing

69
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,670
was the weddings I hosted before

70
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,910
weren't this grand.

71
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,750
This time,
there were so many celebrities.

72
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,470
(Starstruck online)
So I was a little nervous.

73
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,270
You two are...

74
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,380
(One of the most in-sync thief duos)
the Sync Bandits?

75
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:01,200
(Caught!)

76
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,470
It's just another side job of mine.

77
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,230
Another side job.

78
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,830
Okay.

79
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,670
The first time, I got

80
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,030
to meet my idols face-to-face.

81
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,150
Stepping off the comedy stage

82
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:10,840
and taking on a new
role in a variety show,

83
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,340
what's the difference?

84
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,990
I had to tone down my performance.

85
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,230
On the comedy stage,

86
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,790
I had to be more exaggerated.

87
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,020
(Shixiang: A crosstalk term)
It means using exaggerated acting

88
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:21,680
(meaning the actor has to use)
to portray the character,

89
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,260
(exaggerated expressions and mannerisms)
but this time,

90
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:22,880
(for comedic effect)
I had to keep it real.

91
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,000
First, I didn't want
to scare our guests.

92
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,990
Second,

93
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:27,180
it was mainly

94
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,290
to keep things

95
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:29,470
running smoothly.

96
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,090
And

97
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,490
for the comedy,

98
00:02:32,490 --> 00:02:33,390
I'll leave that to

99
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:34,650
my senior, Jin.

100
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:36,630
(If you get the chance)
Who'd you recommend for The Truth?

101
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,150
I'd definitely pick Wang Tianfang first.

102
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,190
Because normally,

103
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:41,970
he's

104
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:42,360
pretty...

105
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:43,320
low-key.

106
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,440
He doesn't like joining activities.

107
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,700
Actually, it's because he's timid.

108
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,270
This is exactly what scares him most.

109
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:47,750
anything

110
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:50,270
even slightly scary.

111
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,030
When he comes on,

112
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,590
it'll be great to watch.

113
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:53,450
Really great.

114
00:02:53,450 --> 00:02:54,520
Really funny.

115
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,950
I once did an escape room with him,

116
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,350
and seeing how he reacted,

117
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,030
he never opened his eyes
the entire time.

118
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,950
Any little sound

119
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:01,990
and he'd get scared.

120
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:03,510
So I really want to see

121
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,670
how he'd react when scared.

122
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,550
Because we know the others pretty well,

123
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,270
and they're all pretty comfortable

124
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,790
with deduction and all that.

125
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,990
But he's

126
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:10,470
really timid.

127
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,430
(So scared)
It's nothing

128
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,830
like his tough-guy image.

129
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:14,830
He's actually incredibly timid.

130
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,350
So I'd definitely
recommend Wang Tianfang.

131
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,830
When you played the dead body,

132
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:21,520
lying in the chair
while everyone watched,

133
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,830
(Zhang Xuzhen as An Er)
what was going through your mind?

134
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,150
How should I put it?

135
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:24,750
It's just that...

136
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,670
I felt like they were messing with me.

137
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,270
At first,

138
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:29,950
when I was sitting there,

139
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,430
right after they found me,

140
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,430
Detective Ning,

141
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:34,160
was about to

142
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,470
search my body.

143
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:36,760
He was this close.

144
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,790
As the dead man,

145
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,910
I almost ended up disheveled.

146
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,390
I thought they might strip me
down completely,

147
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,390
even my shoes,

148
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,670
and the lining of my shirt.

149
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,470
Luckily, thanks to

150
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,790
Detective Ning's guidance,

151
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,310
in the end,

152
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:48,960
it was just a needle,

153
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,630
so I managed

154
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:51,340
(Just a tiny needle)
to stay fully intact.

155
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,070
I died all the way to the end.

156
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:55,700
Your beard accidentally
fell off during filming.

157
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,820
How did you feel?

158
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,230
(Pupils shaking)
I was absolutely devastated.

159
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,940
That beard had already been

160
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:02,780
hanging on for dear life

161
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,030
(Loose beard)
when I was walking downstairs with Yi.

162
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,830
The moment we stepped outside,
it started falling off.

163
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:06,560
(Beard left halfway through the scene)

164
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,830
At that point, my mind

165
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,030
had completely gone blank.

166
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,430
My head was a total mess.

167
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,390
After we went downstairs,

168
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,270
I could barely even hear

169
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,070
what they were saying.

170
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:16,920
(Ended up amusing himself)

171
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,910
I instinctively greeted everyone,

172
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:19,870
then we started taking photos.

173
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:20,550
Then Ke Yu told me

174
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:22,290
my beard had fallen off.

175
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:23,480
(My world collapsed)
At that point...

176
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,110
at that point,
I couldn't even respond to him.

177
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,510
All I could think was,

178
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,470
What do I do?

179
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,350
And he was really sweet.

180
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,710
(Warm-hearted An Ke)
He helped me put my beard back on.

181
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,070
I didn't even know how to respond,

182
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:33,620
so it

183
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,990
was a bit unfortunate.

184
00:04:36,050 --> 00:04:37,860
What was it like playing your
good friend Zhou Keyu's older brother?

185
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:38,960
What stood out to you?

186
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,830
Mostly, it just felt

187
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,750
(Ke, you feel so familiar)
really familiar.

188
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,670
We've worked together before,

189
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:43,690
so this time

190
00:04:43,690 --> 00:04:44,880
(Source: Internet)
was our second time

191
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,030
meeting on a variety show.

192
00:04:46,030 --> 00:04:46,760
(Is it Uncle Ke?)

193
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:47,590
It felt really familiar.

194
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,550
(It's Er)
Just seeing him

195
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,550
felt like I was back on set,

196
00:04:51,550 --> 00:04:52,160
spending time

197
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:52,910
together

198
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,430
just like we used to.

199
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:54,910
It was really nice.

200
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,190
(Huang Jin as An Ke's crazy mom)
You scared Wang Yuwen earlier.

201
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,490
Anything you'd like to say to her?

202
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,500
(Young heart deeply traumatized)

203
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,590
I'm really sorry.

204
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,620
I've been scared before too,

205
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:10,600
and it feels awful.

206
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:11,970
It's all fake,

207
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:12,740
Wen.

208
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:13,200
It's all fake.

209
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:13,990
Don't believe it.

210
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:15,450
But you

211
00:05:15,450 --> 00:05:16,580
should really listen, look, and feel it.

212
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,470
It's great.

213
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:20,470
When you reunited with your
character's child, An Ke,

214
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:21,780
how did you feel?

215
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,990
Feels strangely familiar.

216
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:27,040
Yeah.

217
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,510
It felt like this person

218
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,790
had always been part of my life,

219
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:31,740
but at the same time,

220
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,620
I wasn't sure if he really existed.

221
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,210
But...

222
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:35,530
when

223
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:37,430
I hugged him,

224
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:38,740
I still felt like

225
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:40,490
this son of mine

226
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,000
should be by my side.

227
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,670
It felt really warm.

228
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,520
It was a sense of

229
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,160
companionship.

230
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:46,520
Yeah.

231
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:47,680
At that moment,

232
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:50,390
it felt like the pain of being beaten

233
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:54,550
finally had some comfort,
some consolation.

234
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:57,110
Maybe it made me stronger

235
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,070
to protect...

236
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,510
the children who were being hurt.

237
00:06:00,510 --> 00:06:02,260
(Companionship gives me strength
to protect those around me)

238
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,370
=The Truth (Season 4)=

239
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:06,500
(SVIP: New episodes Wed & Thu at 12 PM)

240
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,660
(VIP: Next-day access at 12 PM,
one week early)
